#### Fitering VCF file ####

Filtering a VCF file is done to remove low-confidence or biologically unreliable variants before population genetic analysis.
Raw variant calling usually contains:
sequencing errors
alignment artifacts
PCR errors
poorly genotyped loci
extremely rare suspicious variants
filtering improves the reliability of your SNP dataset.

## General idea ##

Variant calling is probabilistic.
The caller is essentially saying: “I think this position is a SNP.”

Filtering applies additional quality criteria to keep only trustworthy variants.

### filters explained ###

1. minQ30
This filters variants based on variant quality score (QUAL).

What QUAL means
QUAL estimates confidence that the variant is real rather than sequencing noise.

It is Phred-scaled:
Q = -10 log10(error probability)
What Q30 means
Q30 → error probability = 0.001

Meaning:
~99.9% confidence
expected false call rate ≈ 1 in 1000

Why filter by QUAL?
Low QUAL variants often arise from:
sequencing errors
poor alignments
low coverage
repetitive regions

Removing low-quality SNPs reduces false positives.

2. minGQ30
This filters genotypes based on genotype quality (GQ).

Difference between QUAL and GQ
Metric	          Applies to
QUAL	       entire variant site
GQ	       genotype of each individual

Example
Suppose a SNP exists at one position.
The site itself may be real (high QUAL), but one individual may have uncertain genotype because of low coverage.

Example:
| Individual | Genotype | GQ |
| Bat1 | AA | 99 |
| Bat2 | AG | 12 |
| Bat3 | GG | 85 |
Bat2 genotype is uncertain.

## Why GQ filtering matters ##
Low GQ genotypes can introduce:
false heterozygotes
artificial population structure
incorrect allele frequencies

Filtering removes unreliable genotype calls.

3. Remove indels
Removes insertions and deletions. Keeps only SNPs.

## Why remove indels? ##

Indels are harder to call accurately because:
alignment becomes complicated
repetitive regions create artifacts
indels often have higher error rates

For ddRAD population genetics, SNPs are usually preferred because they are:
abundant
easier to analyze
more reliable

4. remove-filtered-all
Removes variants that failed filters during variant calling.

What is FILTER column?
VCF contains:
FILTER coloumn and it has these possible values:
Value           	Meaning
PASS      	   passed caller filters
LowQual	       low confidence
other tags    	caller-specific issues

## Why remove filtered variants? ##
The variant caller itself already flagged some variants as suspicious.
Keeping them may increase false positives.

5. mac3
MAC = Minor Allele Count.

Requires the minor allele to appear at least 3 times across all samples.
Example
Individual	  Genotype
  1	             AA
  2	             AA
  3	             AA
  4              AG
Minor allele = G
Total G copies = 1
This SNP would fail MAC3.

## Why use MAC filtering? ##

Very rare alleles are often:
sequencing errors
PCR artifacts
poorly supported variants.

Rare variants can also distort analyses like PCA/admixture.
MAC filtering increases robustness.

6. hwe 0.05
Filters variants that strongly deviate from Hardy–Weinberg equilibrium.

What is Hardy–Weinberg equilibrium?
Under random mating, genotype frequencies should approximately follow:
p² + 2pq + q² = 1

## Why SNPs deviate from HWE ##
Possible reasons:
Cause	                                 Biological or technical
sequencing/alignment error	                 technical
paralogous loci                            	technical
population structure	                      biological
selection	                                  biological
inbreeding	                                biological

## Why use HWE filtering? ##
In population genomics, extreme deviations are often caused by technical artifacts.
Especially in RAD/ddRAD data:
paralog mapping
allele dropout
misalignments
can create false heterozygotes.

### Important caution ###
Since you have multiple species, HWE filtering can be tricky.
Pooling species together causes strong HWE deviations naturally because allele frequencies differ among species.
This is called the: Wahlund effect

So HWE filtering should ideally be done:
within populations/species
not across all species combined
Otherwise true biological differentiation may be removed.

7. imiss
removing individuals with high missing data.

## What it measures ##
Fraction of missing genotypes per individual.
Example:
Individual	Missing rate
Bat1	           2%
Bat2	           40%
Bat3	           5%
Bat2 is poor quality.

8. max-missing
Requires variants to be present in a minimum fraction of samples.

Example
Suppose in 10 individuals:
SNP present in	    Missingness
10/10	                 0%
8/10	                 20%
2/10	                 80% missing

With:
--max-missing 0.8
the SNP must exist in at least 80% of individuals.

# Example #
Suppose a SNP site looks like this:
Individual	Genotype
1	             AA
2	             AA
3	             AG
4	             AA
5	             GG
6	             AA
7            	 AA
8	             AA
9	            ./.
10	          ./.
Here:
8 individuals have genotype data
2 are missing (./.)
So:
8/10 = 0.8
This SNP passes --max-missing 0.8

# Another example #
Individual	Genotype
1	             AA
2	             AG
3	             ./.
4	             ./.
5	             GG
6	             ./.
7	             AA
8	             ./.
9	             AA
10	           ./.
Only 5 individuals have genotype calls.
5/10 = 0.5
This SNP would be removed.

## Why this matters in ddRAD ##
ddRAD datasets often contain many loci missing in some individuals because:
restriction sites mutate
uneven sequencing depth
allele dropout
inconsistent digestion

So --max-missing helps keep loci that are consistently represented across samples.

######## Overall purpose of your filtering pipeline ######

Your filters are trying to keep variants that are:
confidently called
reliably genotyped
sufficiently represented
biologically meaningful
minimally affected by technical artifacts

## Simplified interpretation of your pipeline ##
Filter	                       Removes
minQ30	                  low-confidence SNPs
minGQ30	                 uncertain genotypes
remove indels	            complicated variants
remove-filtered-all	       caller-flagged variants
mac3	                 ultra-rare suspicious alleles
hwe 0.05	               abnormal loci/artifacts
imiss	                    poor-quality individuals
max-missing	               poorly represented SNPs


























































  
  













  




